## 1. Executive Escalation Summary

This simulated case concerns a hydraulic cylinder that reportedly moves without load but slows and stalls under its usual operating load.

The customer reports that the electric motor continues running and no external leakage is visible from the normal operating position.

The problem reportedly appeared after recent maintenance. A technician also reports an abnormal pressure indication, but instrument accuracy and operating conditions have not been verified.

**Reason for escalation:** The available evidence is insufficient to identify a failed component or recommend a corrective action.

Engineering assistance is requested to identify the applicable manufacturer-approved diagnostic approach, review the available information, and determine what additional evidence is necessary.

No physical troubleshooting or corrective action has been performed as part of this simulation.

