## 5. Preliminary Technical Assessment

The reported symptom pattern indicates that actuator movement is possible under the described unloaded condition, but the system reportedly cannot complete its intended loaded movement.

The available evidence does not establish whether the problem originates from:

- Mechanical load conditions
- Hydraulic fluid routing
- Hydraulic supply performance
- Maintenance-related configuration changes
- Instrumentation reliability

The continued operation of the electric motor does not independently verify hydraulic pump performance.

The absence of visible external leakage does not rule out internal leakage or other hydraulic performance issues.

The timing of the problem after maintenance warrants review but does not prove that maintenance caused the reported condition.

No specific component failure has been established.

## 6. Working Hypotheses

